# Foundation publishes only the compiled output in .tsbuild/. The `files` list in
# package.json both whitelists that directory and, with `!` entries, drops what tsc emits
# beside the real output: test files, the test support (test-utils, test/setup, which import
# vitest), vitest.config and the tsbuildinfo. Those exclusions must live in `files`: a root
# .npmignore cannot exclude a path that `files` includes.
#
# .gitignore would otherwise be used as a fallback by npm pack — and it
# excludes .tsbuild/ — so this file must exist (even if empty) to prevent
# the published tarball from losing its types.
